    {
      "title": "Module 3: Asking for Directions",
      "subtopics": [
        {
          "title": "3.1 Asking the Way",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "title": "How to Ask for Directions",
              "weight": 5,
              "content": [
                {
                  "order": 1,
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "{\"time\":1700005005000,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"gG8hH9iI0j\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"When you don't know the way somewhere, you can ask someone for directions. Here are polite ways to ask:\"}},{\"id\":\"jJ1kK2lL3m\",\"type\":\"list\",\"data\":{\"style\":\"unordered\",\"items\":[\"<b>Excuse me, where is the bank?</b>\",\"<b>Excuse me, how do I get to the train station?</b>\",\"<b>Could you tell me the way to the park?</b>\",\"<b>Is there a supermarket near here?</b>\"]}},{\"id\":\"mM4nN5oO6p\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Always start with <b>Excuse me</b> — it is polite to get someone's attention this way before asking a question.\"}},{\"id\":\"pP7qQ8rR9s\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"If you don't understand, you can say:\"}},{\"id\":\"sS0tT1uU2v\",\"type\":\"list\",\"data\":{\"style\":\"unordered\",\"items\":[\"<b>Could you repeat that, please?</b>\",\"<b>I'm sorry, I don't understand.</b>\",\"<b>Can you speak more slowly, please?</b>\"]}}],\"version\":\"2.31.4\"}"
                },
                {
                  "order": 2,
                  "type": "audio",
                  "content": {
                    "text": "Excuse me! How do I get to the train station?",
                    "type": "tts",
                    "audio_url": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "order": 3,
                  "type": "speech-recognition",
                  "content": {
